<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ meta.mainLanguage }}">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" />
    <title>WriteFlow Google Sheets Setup</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/write-platform.css" />
  </head>
  <body class="dw-body wp-theme--light">
    <div class="dw-shell dw-stack" style="max-width:720px;padding-top:32px;">
      <a class="dw-link" href="/writeflow/">← WriteFlow Studio</a>
      <div class="dw-card dw-stack">
        <h1 class="dw-h1">Google Sheets setup</h1>
        <p class="dw-lead">Connect WriteFlow to Google Sheets so student submissions sync for any teacher, on any device.</p>
        <ol class="dw-list">
          <li>Create a Google Sheet (e.g. <strong>WriteFlow Submissions</strong>).</li>
          <li>Extensions → Apps Script → paste <code>google-apps-script/writeflow-backend.gs</code> → Save.</li>
          <li>Set <code>SPREADSHEET_ID</code> in the script.</li>
          <li>Run <code>initSheet</code> once (authorize when prompted).</li>
          <li>Deploy → Web app (Execute as: Me, Anyone).</li>
          <li>Vercel env: <code>WRITEFLOW_SCRIPT_URL</code> and <code>WRITEFLOW_API_SECRET</code> (match script <code>API_SECRET</code>).</li>
          <li>Redeploy the site.</li>
        </ol>
        <h2 class="dw-h2">Teacher workflow</h2>
        <ul class="dw-list">
          <li>Build assignment in <a href="/writeflow/?mode=builder">WriteFlow builder</a>.</li>
          <li>Set a <strong>teacher password</strong> and click Save — registers assignment in the sheet.</li>
          <li>Share student link: <code>/writeflow/?id=YOUR-ID</code></li>
          <li>View results with the same password via <strong>Results</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
